<h1><span class="mw-headline" id="Entries">Entries</span></h1>
<p>This contest is a little different entry procedure than others.
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Submitting_an_entry">Submitting an entry</span></h3>
<ul><li> Join the <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://social.bioware.com/group/2535">Community Contest Group</a></li>
<li> Add your MRH and MOR file to a .7z or .zip file</li>
<li> Name the file "Character Name - Entrant Name.zip"</li>
<li> upload the file to the <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://social.bioware.com/project/3410/">Mini Contest project</a>. Ensure it is "Viewable by everyone"</li>
<li> upload a screenshot and make an entry on this Contest Page (below)</li></ul>
<p>For general contest entry FAQs please see the <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Community%20Contest%20Entry%20FAQ" title="Community Contest Entry FAQ">Entry FAQs</a>. Note that some may not apply to this mini contest.
</p><p>For information on Judging, please see the <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Community%20Contest%20Judging" title="Community Contest Judging">Judging</a> page.
</p>
<pre><font size="5" color="red"><b><u>IMPORTANT - consent to share</u></b></font>

<font color="red"><b>By entering this competition you consent to share your work for other community members to benefit from.
Where appropriate, source files should be shared (include the MRH head morph). 
The work *MUST* be your own (obviously you may use DA assets).
Do not use custom hair/textures/voicework etc unless you have explicit consent from the author to share. You must include them with your submission.
Others may use and modify your work in their Dragon Age mods, though are encouraged to give credit. 
As the entries are judged, local copies will be saved If your work is taken down.
If your work is taken down, you allow for it to be re-uploaded, crediting the work in your name. </b> </font>
</pre>
